  <!-- MinimumOSVersion for App.framework.

       Raised 13.0 -> 15.0 for ITMS-90068: from spring 2027 Apple stops
       accepting builds whose minimum is below 15.0.

       MEASURED, 3.41.9: this key does NOT control the built framework.
       With 15.0 here and IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 15.0, the produced
       build/ios/iphoneos/Runner.app/Frameworks/App.framework still reports
       MinimumOSVersion 13.0, because the tool compiles it with
       -miphoneos-version-min=FlutterDarwinPlatform.ios.deploymentTarget(),
       hardcoded to Version(13, 0) in
       packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/darwin/darwin.dart:62. The prebuilt
       Flutter.framework is 13.0 for the same reason.

       What Apple reads for the app's minimum is the APP bundle's Info.plist
       and the binary's LC_BUILD_VERSION, both of which are 15.0. Embedded
       frameworks declaring a LOWER minimum than the host app are normal.

       The real sources of truth are IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 15.0 in
       project.pbxproj and `platform :ios, '15.0'` in the Podfile. Flutter's
       migration deletes this key on some builds; that is not a regression. -->
  <key>MinimumOSVersion</key>
  <string>15.0</string>
</dict>
</plist>
